AI Edge Model Explorer Visualizer
https://www.npmjs.com/package/ai-edge-model-explorer-visualizer
https://github.com/google-ai-edge/model-explorer

TraceLens loads ai-edge-model-explorer-visualizer 0.1.2 the way that
package's README describes:

  * the <model-explorer-visualizer> component comes from
    https://unpkg.com/ai-edge-model-explorer-visualizer@0.1.2
  * font textures and styles come from
    https://unpkg.com/ai-edge-model-explorer-visualizer@0.1.2/dist/static_files
    (modelExplorer.assetFilesBaseUrl; another origin is allowed)
  * dist/worker.js is served from this same origin as ./worker.js
    (modelExplorer.workerScriptPath). The package README states that a
    worker loaded from a different origin is not supported.

The published package names its author as Google Inc. and its license as
Apache-2.0. Its source carries this notice:

